handoff/DECIDED.md:121:### d28 · What colour is the placeholder text in the field?
handoff/DECIDED.md:123:- tokens.color.content.placeholder (web --tm-content-placeholder): `.tm-field__control ::placeholder { color: var(--tm-content-placeholder); }` — *Source: Design system*
handoff/DECIDED.md:136:### o13 · Which token is the busy spinner's ring?
handoff/DECIDED.md:138:- The busy spinner ring uses `--tm-content-inverse` instead of `#fff` (same white). — *Source: D-98*
handoff/DECIDED.md:139:- Ring width tokens.spinner.ring, colour tokens.color.content.inverse, box tokens.spinner.size: `border: var(--tm-spinner-ring) solid var(--tm-content-inverse)` — *Source: Design system*
handoff/DECIDED.md:160:### d29 · Border widths, the focus ring, icon and spinner sizes and the logo width: are there tokens?
handoff/DECIDED.md:162:- (1) Sizes the Sign-in kit found with no token become design-system tokens (border width, focus ring width and offset, logo lockup width, icon sizes incl. the notice icon 20, spinner size and ring), listed in as `[PROPOSED]`. — *Source: D-98*
handoff/DECIDED.md:163:- tokens.borderWidth.default, tokens.focusRing.width / .offset, tokens.iconSize.sm / .md / .lg, tokens.spinner.size / .ring, tokens.logoLockup.width. The +91 prefix is messages['signin.phonePrefix']; the logo's accessible name is messages['signin.logoAlt']. — *Source: Tokens*
handoff/DECIDED.md:179:- L2 — Loading primary buttons: brand-blue fill, white label, white spinner, on every screen (sign-in "Sending OTP", OTP "Verifying", any future loading primary). — *Source: Design rules L2*
handoff/DECIDED.md:180:- **States:** pressed; disabled (design-system disabled style, exempt from contrast); busy (L2). Busy spinner → label gap is 8 on every busy button. A quiet action in progress shows text only ("Ending…"), no spinner. **Busy labels always end with "…"** ("Verifying…", "Sending OTP…") (D-54). — *Source: Design rules 9.1*
handoff/DECIDED.md:191:- Minutes are not capped, so 75 minutes shows 75:00; the time is rounded up, so it never shows 0:00 while waiting: `return `${Math.floor(s / 60)}:${String(s % 60).padStart(2, "0")}`;` — *Source: Sign-in build*
handoff/DECIDED.md:200:- **Decision:** OTP issue cap is configurable. Start at 4 codes per mobile number in a server-enforced limit window, counting initial code and up to 3 resends. Do not reset count when the doctor restarts sign-in or changes number and returns. — *Source: D-35*
handoff/DECIDED.md:356:- Code life and issue window 10 min (`otpWindow`), number lock 15 min after the 5th server-confirmed wrong code (`otpLock`, D-34), resend waits 30 s → 1 min → 2 min (`resendWaits`), 4 codes per window (D-35). `[MOCK ASSUMPTION]` — *Source: Prototype setting [MOCK]*
handoff/DECIDED.md:365:- The server sends the time the wait ends; the prototype uses otpWindow, otpLock, resendWaits, tooManyTriesWait as stand-ins (mock values, not product promises). — *Source: Sign-in build*
handoff/DECIDED.md:371:### o03 · Send OTP again for the same number while the resend wait is still running: what does the server answer?
handoff/DECIDED.md:425:- Terms → `https://www.truemeds.in/legal/terms-and-conditions`, Privacy → `https://www.truemeds.in/legal/privacy-policy` (placeholders, linked from the live Terms page), configurable from the server, not typed into the app. — *Source: D-101*
handoff/DECIDED.md:499:### o24 · How fast does the busy spinner turn, and does it stop when the phone's reduce-motion setting is on?
handoff/DECIDED.md:503:- Use `tokens.duration.spinner` (800 ms): the web turns it once every 0.8 s and stops it under reduce motion. — *Source: Prototype*
handoff/DECIDED.md:509:### o25 · "New to Truemeds?" and "Sign up" are two copy entries; the space between them is typed in code. One entry with a {link} placeholder instead?
handoff/DECIDED.md:511:- "New to Truemeds? Sign up" becomes one copy entry with a `{link}` placeholder. — *Source: D-101*
handoff/DECIDED.md:526:- **Confirmed 2026-10-12:** Signed-in session remains valid until the case is closed; no OTP prompt over a live case. Technical token renewal must not interrupt the doctor. Re-authentication after case closure remains open; the 24 h session value above is only a mock placeholder. — *Source: OQ-017*
