handoff/DECIDED.md:588:- **Verify never moves:** one line is reserved under the code boxes. Every state with a one-line message (wrong code, tries left, new code sent, code expired, empty or too short, resend, cooldown) shows its message there, or nothing; Verify & sign in keeps the same place. Notice-box states (offline, locked, couldn't verify, resend failed, too many codes) may move it; accepted. — *Source: App logic §2.*
handoff/DECIDED.md:609:- **5** server-confirmed wrong codes lock **that mobile number** (not the account) `[LOCKED D-34]`. Lock length `[MOCK 15 min, OPEN OQ-017]`. Change number stays available; another number works only if Doctor Ops approved it for this doctor. — *Source: App logic §2.*
handoff/DECIDED.md:616:- **4** codes per number per limit window (first code + 3 resends), not reset by restarting sign-in `[LOCKED D-35]`. Window length `[MOCK 10 min, OPEN OQ-017]`. — *Source: App logic §2.*
handoff/DECIDED.md:623:- Resend waits `[MOCK]` 30 s, then 60 s, then 120 s. Resend line hidden when resends are used up or the number is locked. — *Source: App logic §2.*
handoff/DECIDED.md:658:- otp.default: None — Keyboard open on load; box 1 focused; resend timer running (D-44) — *Source: Feedback state map: otp.default*
handoff/DECIDED.md:698:### otp-19 · What does the app show in otp.resend-available, and how does it recover?
handoff/DECIDED.md:700:- otp.resend-available: None — "Resend code" brand link, 44pt tap area, under the notice (D-44) — *Source: Feedback state map: otp.resend-available*
handoff/DECIDED.md:707:- otp.new-code-sent: S1 — Confirmed resend; restart countdown — *Source: Feedback state map: otp.new-code-sent*
handoff/DECIDED.md:721:- otp.couldnt-verify: F2 — Retain code; resend line shown (D-44) — *Source: Feedback state map: otp.couldnt-verify*
handoff/DECIDED.md:726:### otp-23 · What does the app show in otp.too-many-resends, and how does it recover?
handoff/DECIDED.md:728:- otp.too-many-resends: W1 — Resend line hidden; last unexpired code can still verify — *Source: Feedback state map: otp.too-many-resends*
handoff/DECIDED.md:733:### otp-24 · What does the app show in otp.resending, and how does it recover?
handoff/DECIDED.md:735:- otp.resending: L1 on Resend — One resend pending; keep current challenge until response; prevent duplicates — *Source: Feedback state map: otp.resending*
