handoff/DECIDED.md:1519:- Transfer ready (`call.transfer-ready` 12) — Script stays (call still live): **Confirm & transfer** · Skip HA — shown only once the backend confirms gate time since the patient answered and the call is live (D-58 pt 14) · Blocked — *Source: App logic §4.*
handoff/DECIDED.md:1526:- Call not valid (`call.ended-early` 6, `call.result-missing` 7d) — No script — the call has ended (D-58 pt 24): 6: notice · **Call again** · Callback (no Unavailable, D-58 pt 23) · 7d (Cat4): notice · **Confirm prescription** · Callback + Unavailable (reason sheet, D-75) · 7d (Pilot): **Confirm & forward** · Callback + Unavailable, no Skip HA · Blocked — *Source: App logic §4.*
handoff/DECIDED.md:1533:- Valid, call ended (`call.valid` 8a / 8b) — No script — the call has ended (D-58 pt 24): 8a: **Confirm prescription** only · 8b: **Confirm & forward** · ⏭ **Skip HA** full width (only when allowed, §6). No Callback · Blocked — *Source: App logic §4.*
handoff/DECIDED.md:1659:- **Before the gate, never show:** Confirm prescription, Confirm & transfer, Confirm & forward, Skip HA. — *Source: App logic §5.*
handoff/DECIDED.md:1771:- 7d — `call.result-missing`: Result not received · Backend check found nothing; the call has ended · Amber notice · Cat4: **Confirm prescription** · Callback + Unavailable · Pilot (`s7d-result-missing-pilot`): **Confirm & forward** · Callback + Unavailable · no Skip HA. Unavailable opens the reason sheet (D-75); **the chosen reason is saved with the case** for Ops monitoring (D-73) · `s7d-result-missing` / `s7d-result-missing-pilot` — *Source: App logic §5.*
handoff/DECIDED.md:1799:- 8b — `call.valid`: Valid call (forward) · Same · Confirm & forward · Skip HA (full width) · no Callback · no script · `t08b-valid-forward` — *Source: App logic §5.*
handoff/DECIDED.md:1806:- 8c — `case.confirm-blocked`: Confirm tapped with Pending medicines · Tap on any confirm button while a medicine is Pending (Flag 5) · Confirm prescription only, plus a red line "Prescribe or disable {n} medicines first."; page scrolls to the first Pending medicine; button stays tappable; no Callback · `t08c-confirm-blocked` — *Source: App logic §5.*
handoff/DECIDED.md:1841:- 12 — `call.transfer-ready`: Confirm & transfer · Backend: gate time since `customerAnswered`, call live · Confirm & transfer · Skip HA (full width) · no Callback · `t12-transfer-ready` — *Source: App logic §5.*
handoff/DECIDED.md:1848:- 13 — —: Transferring · Tap on Confirm & transfer · "Transferring…" busy · Skip HA greyed and disabled (full width, K13) · no Callback · `t13-connecting-ha` — *Source: App logic §5.*
handoff/DECIDED.md:1883:- 16 — `call.transfer-missed`: Ended before the transfer · Ozonetel hang-up after the gate, not transferred · Amber notice naming who ended the call (doctor / patient / unknown) · Confirm & forward · Skip HA · no script · `t16-transfer-missed` (doctor) · `t16b-…-patient` · `t16c-…-unknown` — *Source: App logic §5.*
handoff/DECIDED.md:1888:### case-57 · What happens in "call.skip-ha-wait" (state 17)?
handoff/DECIDED.md:1890:- 17 — `call.skip-ha-wait`: Skip HA during a transfer call · Skip HA confirmed · Grey "Health Advisor call will be skipped. End the call when you’re done." (`call.skipHa`, D-85) · status line "Getting call result…" only (no "Calling {name}…", no buttons, no header Back), then Confirm prescription on the result · no Callback · `t17-skip-ha-wait` — *Source: App logic §5.*
handoff/DECIDED.md:1939:- **Launch = Fallback B (D-83, D-85).** Pilot live call → **Confirm prescription** (B1) → B2 checks for an HA → free: Transferring → **Transferred** (14) · none: **Forwarded** (B3). Pilot call ended before Confirm (16) or 7d → **Confirm & forward**. Skip HA → 17 → result path → Confirm prescription. Non-Value Meds go through the same HA check. The table below is **version A (later)**, where the route is known at call start. — *Source: App logic §6.*
handoff/DECIDED.md:1951:### case-66 · What happens in "HA skipped (by customer, system, or the doctor's Skip HA)"?
handoff/DECIDED.md:1953:- Pilot — HA skipped (by customer, system, or the doctor's Skip HA): Confirm prescription · Prescription confirmed — *Source: App logic §6.*
handoff/DECIDED.md:1974:- **7d follows the route (D-83):** Cat4 / HA skipped → **Confirm prescription**; Pilot with an HA call → **Confirm & forward** (the transfer is no longer possible once the call has ended). Secondaries: **Callback + Unavailable**; no Skip HA on 7d. **Skip HA** on 8b, 12 and 16 sits full width under the main button (D-83, K1). — *Source: App logic §6.*
handoff/DECIDED.md:1979:### case-70 · What is the rule for "Skip HA"?
handoff/DECIDED.md:1981:- **Skip HA** only after the gate, for **both Pilot types** (Value and Non-Value Meds) whenever an HA call follows the doctor call and it isn't already skipped — no other conditions (D-59). Opens the reason sheet: Patient declined HA call · Clinically not required · Repeat patient, familiar with the medicines — Counselled in an earlier order (D-70 item 3; title and sub-line). Choosing a reason applies it at once. On a call with a result the final button becomes **Confirm prescription**; during a live transfer call the case then waits for the call result (state 17, D-58 point 14). Skip HA is also offered after a missed transfer (state 16, D-58 point 24). — *Source: App logic §6.*
handoff/DECIDED.md:2014:### case-75 · What is the rule for "✅ Flag 5"?
handoff/DECIDED.md:2016:- ✅ **Flag 5 — answered:** Confirm is blocked while any medicine is Pending. The button stays tappable; on tap a notice in the bar says "Prescribe or disable {n} medicines first." and the page scrolls to the first Pending medicine. Applies to all three confirm buttons; Callback, Skip HA and Unavailable stay allowed. — *Source: App logic §6.*
handoff/DECIDED.md:2084:### case-85 · What is the rule for "✅ Flag 6"?
handoff/DECIDED.md:2086:- ✅ **Flag 6 — answered:** the case does go back to the queue, but the doctor is not told — no queue line anywhere. **Updated D-83:** the case goes on hold and the system retries it by hangup cause; nothing goes to Ops. — *Source: App logic §7.*
handoff/DECIDED.md:2156:- **Busy states.** Busy bars keep their height and the button's place: Transferring… keeps the Skip HA row, greyed and disabled, with no Callback (D-83 K13); Confirming… keeps its row. The status line takes the buttons' row in the confirm fallback (B2). 7c shows the same screen as 5 at normal bar height — no empty tray (D-91). The end-of-call script card has 16 padding below in every state. — *Source: App logic §13*
handoff/DECIDED.md:2247:- case.release-failed: F2 — Sheet closes over Ready; doctor stays on the case; error notice "Couldn't release this case. You're still on it. Try again."; Back works again. *Copy approved (D-53).* (D-81 F22) — *Source: Feedback state map: case.release-failed*
handoff/DECIDED.md:2296:- call.skipHa: Grey note in the bar — "Health Advisor call will be skipped. End the call when you’re done." on 17 (`t17-skip-ha-wait`), with the no-HA script and the status line "Getting call result…" (D-85). No Calling line, no buttons. — *Source: Feedback state map: call.skipHa*
handoff/DECIDED.md:2310:- case.result-missing-pilot: Same as 7d — Pilot 7d: "We didn’t get the call result." notice; **Confirm & forward** · Callback + Unavailable; no Skip HA (D-83). — *Source: Feedback state map: case.result-missing-pilot*
handoff/DECIDED.md:2359:- [MOCK] 15 min in the prototype. Keep configurable (a server or config value, never typed into a screen); not a production promise. Note: gap between retries; Engineering to agree. — *Source: Prototype setting [MOCK]*
