191:- Minutes are not capped, so 75 minutes shows 75:00; the time is rounded up, so it never shows 0:00 while waiting: `return `${Math.floor(s / 60)}:${String(s % 60).padStart(2, "0")}`;` — *Source: Sign-in build*
356:- Code life and issue window 10 min (`otpWindow`), number lock 15 min after the 5th server-confirmed wrong code (`otpLock`, D-34), resend waits 30 s → 1 min → 2 min (`resendWaits`), 4 codes per window (D-35). `[MOCK ASSUMPTION]` — *Source: Prototype setting [MOCK]*
365:- The server sends the time the wait ends; the prototype uses otpWindow, otpLock, resendWaits, tooManyTriesWait as stand-ins (mock values, not product promises). — *Source: Sign-in build*
565:| [otp-31](#otp-31) | Limits and timings | What is the value of "resendWaits"? |
609:- **5** server-confirmed wrong codes lock **that mobile number** (not the account) `[LOCKED D-34]`. Lock length `[MOCK 15 min, OPEN OQ-017]`. Change number stays available; another number works only if Doctor Ops approved it for this doctor. — *Source: App logic §2.*
777:- [MOCK] 15 min in the prototype. Keep configurable (a server or config value, never typed into a screen); not a production promise. Note: OQ-017: lock after 5 wrong codes. — *Source: Prototype setting [MOCK]*
782:### otp-31 · What is the value of "resendWaits"?
1110:- **Set availability:** quick picks 15 / 30 / 45 min, 1 / 2 / 3 hours, plus the wheel (hours and minutes, 15-minute steps). Minimum **15 minutes**, any start time, no maximum (24/7). Confirm starts the countdown. — *Source: App logic §3.*
1131:- **Add time:** shown when time is running low (near expiry, `[MOCK]` 5 min); same picker in a sheet; "Time added" toast. An error in the add-time sheet sits 16 above its button, as on the page. — *Source: App logic §3.*
1334:- [MOCK] 5 min in the prototype. Keep configurable (a server or config value, never typed into a screen); not a production promise. Note: app-logic §3 near-expiry. — *Source: Prototype setting [MOCK]*
1341:- 15 min. Agreed rule (app-logic §3). Read it from configuration; copy reads the value, never a typed number. — *Source: Setting (agreed rule)*
1348:- 15 min. Agreed rule (app-logic §3 (15-min wheel)). Read it from configuration; copy reads the value, never a typed number. — *Source: Setting (agreed rule)*
